WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.368
-Our next guest is
a talented actress you know

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.270
from shows such as
"Big Little Lies"

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.438
and "The Society."

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.807
She stars as Cassie Lang
in the highly-anticipated

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.676
"Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania,"

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.845
which will be in theaters
and IMAX this Friday.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.213
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.082
-You know I promised your mom
that you would only use

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.884
this stuff
when one of us was around.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.152
It's really dangerous tech.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.620
-I know it's dangerous.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.954
-What if the cops took it
from you, huh?

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:22.955
What if you lost it?

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.524
-I didn't lose the suit.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.326
-You have a suit?
Wait, you have a suit?

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.028
-I know how to take care
of myself, okay.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:31.164
Trust me.
I'm pretty good at it by now.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.199
-Ouch.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.735
-Look, I didn't mean it
like that.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:36.769
-I know.
-And I'm sorry.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.105
-It's okay. It's all right.
I get it.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.808
I just think you should get
to have a normal life.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.744
-Dad, a guy dressed like a bee
tried to kill me in my room

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.546
when I was 6.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.380
I've never had a normal life.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.316
-Please welcome back to
the show, Kathryn Newton,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.484
everybody.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.487
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.487 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
♪♪

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.835
-Welcome!
-Hi. Thank you.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.570
-You look wonderful.
-Thank you.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.104
Hi, everyone.
-This is a very exciting week

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:13.706
for you last week.
-Yes.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.409
-The film premiere party,
the launch.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.544
-Yeah.
-Then you also had a birthday.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.146
Happy birthday. Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.448
Thank you.
-Happy birthday.

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.917
-I know, I feel
like I have never celebrated

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.219
my birthday so much.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.687
-Oh, because everywhere
you went --

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.021
-It was my birthday.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:31.691
The premiere was more
my birthday than my birthday,

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.526
you know.
I got the job, you know,

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.827
what, a year and a half ago now?

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.529
And that was like my birthday.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.364
And then, you know,
they celebrated my birthday

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.599
on the press tour.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.400
Everyone surprised me
on my birthday.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.535
I had to go to Toronto
for a premiere,

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:46.039
and the whole audience sang me
happy birthday.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.041
So if you want to, too,
like, I won't --

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:51.811
-I feel like it's a week ago
and I feel like we shouldn't.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.880
-No, no. If you --
No, it's okay.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.216
It's okay.
Thank you so much.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.718
I know you wanted to,
but it's fine.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.086
-Do you like attention
on your birthday?

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.620
Because you're certainly
giving out that vibe.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.122
-No, no.
-No?

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.390
-No, I don't.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.326
Your birthday is, like,
the one day you feel like

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:09.128
everyone has to tell you
happy birthday.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.997
So you -- I feel like you don't
really like me,

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.198
you just are acting like
you like me.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.332
-You wouldn't want them
to say it on other days.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.268
-[ Laughs ] I don't know.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.802
I mean, that never happened
to me before.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:17.837
-That's true.
-Yeah, I've never --

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.205
-We should start doing that
more.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.840
-Just happy birthday, Seth.
-I feel like it's crazy --

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.674
-Yeah, happy birthday to you.
-Thank you.

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:24.577
-It's lovely to hear --
and I feel like I don't know why

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.844
we've kind of, like,
boxed ourselves

00:02:25.844 --> 00:02:28.480
into only saying it on the day.
-Right.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.349
Why would you do that?
-Yeah, why would you do that.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.018
-When you could it say it
every day.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.620
-Also it's fun because
now we share a birthday.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.255
-Right. We could do it together.
-That's so much fun.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.823
-We can have cake any time
we want.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.292
-Oh my God, this is -- I feel
like you cracked the code here.

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:41.627
This is very exciting.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.295
-I guess the real code is
if you can do a Marvel movie,

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.231
like, every movie, then
it's always your birthday.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.432
-Yeah.
That's the important thing.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.034
-Always.
-I mean, obviously,

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:51.437
a Marvel premiere is a little
unlike any other movie premiere.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.038
-Right.
-Was it a trip to be there?

00:02:53.038 --> 00:02:54.173
-It was insane.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:56.442
I mean, I've been a part
of a fandom before.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.810
I was on a show called
"Supernatural,"

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.379
and the fans are incredible.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.547
That's a real fan base show.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:02.881
-That changed my life.

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:04.884
But then I went
to the Marvel movie premiere,

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.953
and it was, like, huge.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.588
The fans are --
it's a huge family.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:12.325
It's insane.
I saw some little Cassie Langs.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.559
So that was crazy.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.994
-People dressed up
in your costume.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.128
-Yeah.
-That's very exciting.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.796
-It was really exciting.
It felt real.

00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:19.165
That's when it felt real.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:22.501
-Did you feel as though people
treated you differently

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.503
on the set when you were wearing
the costume?

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.105
Let's just take a look
real quick.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.240
Because I feel like -- look,
in the clip, you looked great.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.276
But this is -- I mean, that's,
like, very impressive.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.444
-I look a little different,
huh?

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.811
-Yeah.

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:34.146
Did you enjoy wearing the suit?

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:35.782
-Oh, I love wearing the suit.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.918
Can't you tell that's why I'm in
a Cassie Lang suit?

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.587
I just am not done cosplaying
Cassie Lang.

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:42.888
I did my hair in a ponytail.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:46.659
What I'm trying to say
is I'm a fan of Cassie Lang.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.461
No, definitely people
treated you differently.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.631
Like, they were a little quieter
around me.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.766
-Oh, yeah.
-A little more scared.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.735
-Uh-huh.
-I would be scared.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.936
And everyone looked at me like
it was really me.

00:03:57.936 --> 00:03:59.872
Like, they think that's
who you are all of a sudden

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.307
when you wear the supersuit.
and I promise you,

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:04.576
I fall just the same in
that thing as I do in this.

00:04:04.576 --> 00:04:06.178
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.147
I fell a lot.
-You're a faller.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.548
Everybody says that about you.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:11.483
I'm a tripper. I fall.
I'm just like Cassie.

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:14.420
Like, I was trying to figure out
how to be in a Marvel movie

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.955
and, like, impress everybody,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:19.024
and she's a little young hero
trying to impress her dad.

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:20.392
We're very similar.
-There you go.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:23.096
-Yeah, total messes.
-I would imagine Paul Rudd

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.530
is the perfect person
to spend time with.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.165
Especially on your birthday.
I feel like every time

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.200
I'm with Paul,
I do feel like it's my birthday.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.569
-I know.
That's what I'm saying.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:31.904
You get it.
-Everyday is your birthday.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.405
-Everyday was my birthday
on this movie

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:34.507
because of Paul Rudd.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.742
-Yeah.
-Yeah, he's the best.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:39.912
He gave me a little gift.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.514
It's actually from the movie.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.882
-It's a prop from the film?

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.818
-It's a prop from the film
that I can't tell you about.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.152
-Yeah.
-So...

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:49.322
Is it spoiler based?
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.757
-Or are you worried that Paul
will be arrested

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:52.759
for stealing a prop?

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.927
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.195
-I think both,
now that you mention it.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.496
-Yeah, I think both.
Now that we're talking about it,

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:58.897
I feel like you should not put
that man in danger.

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:00.766
If you're the reason Rudd goes
to jail,

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.168
no one here will forgive you.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.335
-Marvel jail.

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:04.437
-Marvel jail, yeah.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.605
-No, he did.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.739
He made it special,
and I'll keep it forever.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.807
-Okay. Well, that's very lovely.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:11.277
-I've talked in the past about
that you consider yourself

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.212
growing up,
you felt a little nerdy.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:16.448
And then this is both superhero,
which I feel like superheroes

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:19.519
no longer have the sort of
nerd stigma they used to have

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.819
because they're very mainstream.
-Right.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.789
-But also there's a great
element of science to this.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:26.826
So did that scratch the nerd
itch, for lack of a better term?

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.827
-Yeah. Cassie Lang is a genius,
you know?

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:31.296
She's figuring out
the quantum realm and stuff.

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:33.899
So, after I finished the movie,
I didn't have a job.

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:35.000
I was very bored.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.803
So I signed up for
a physics class at UCLA.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.139
[ Laughs ] And I did that.
And I got an "A," thank you.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:43.242
-Wow.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.711
So we're the same once again.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:48.014
-Oh, my God, you're her
and she's you.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.315
You're the same.
-I know.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.150
I'm just really method,
just like Jonathan Majors.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.954
-Did the UCLA students
notice you when you started

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.355
taking their physics class?
-No.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.758
I was hoping someone would.
-Is that safe to say

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.292
that you did not dress
like this?

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.627
-No.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.530
I loved putting my outfits
on, though, for the class.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.832
You know, like, I put on
my little blue light glasses

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:07.933
and, like, a sweater vest.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.368
'Cause I didn't go to college,

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:12.805
so I really was really trying in
my Zoom class to make it real.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.507
And it doesn't have
the same effect.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:15.975
-Yeah.
-No.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.977
-Do you think you dress like --
when you saw the other kids,

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.612
did you think, "I'm dressing
like kids in college now"

00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:23.015
or, "I'm dressing like kids
from '90s movies."

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:26.018
-Definitely '90s movies that
I thought people dressed like

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.019
now and they don't.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:28.687
Everyone was in sweatpants.
-Gotcha.

00:06:28.687 --> 00:06:30.256
-I was the only one
in a collared shirt.

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.024
-Uh-huh. And they were like --
-Yeah. It's okay.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:34.293
-"Oh, my God, that's so sad.
That's an actress."

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.330
-[ Laughs ]
I was acting like a student.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.631
Yeah.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.766
-Can I check in on your dogs,
please?

00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:42.702
-Oh, yes. Thank you. That's
so kind of you to remember.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:43.702
-Well, we've talked about
your dogs.

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:48.240
You have three poodles,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.374
all of whom are so good at
posing for photographs.

00:06:49.374 --> 00:06:52.511
-Yes. That is Jack King,
Ruler of All Floof,

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:53.579
Starlight Rosebud,

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:54.947
Hella-good-boy
Gonna-need-a-big-bank.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.716
And "Ten-Four Ladybird
keep the madness rolling."

00:06:57.716 --> 00:06:59.585
-Okay, now,
what do you call them

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:01.420
if you have to, like,
talk to them quickly?

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.222
-Well, last time,
she really didn't have a name

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:06.091
because she doesn't really
remember it.

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:08.427
So we call her Ladybird
or Little.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:10.863
This is Buddy and that's Jack.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.598
-Yeah.
-And so, what are the ages

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.799
of your dogs here?

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:17.002
-He's about 5, 3, and 2.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:19.138
And one of them
has a very special skill.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.206
Who is the yodeler?

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.774
-The little one
is in love with him,

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.677
and so when he barks a lot,
she likes to sing to him.

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.078
She croons.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.179
She's in love, you know.

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:28.981
She just wants him
to notice her.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.382
It's very romantic.

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:32.485
-And do you feel like he's
barking, do you think she's --

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.820
do you think her crooning
is to calm him down

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.555
or just to, like,
be in duet with him?

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.790
In your head,
what are you picturing?

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.392
-[ Howls ]

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:41.560
[ Laughs ]

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.995
What does that say, you know?

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.665
Like, "I love you. Notice me."
I don't know.

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:46.932
-We actually have videos.
-Oh.

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:49.201
-Should we let the whole
audience decide what this --

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:53.071
this true just sort of
expression of love.

00:07:53.071 --> 00:07:54.473
-The expression,
Valentine's Day.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.976
Happy Valentine's Day.
-Okay, let's see it.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:08:00.012 line:0%
[ Dogs barking ]

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.589
-It really is love.

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:10.789
-Doesn't it feel like love?

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:12.024
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:14.060
-I feel like she's saying,
"What you're looking for

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.328
isn't out there.

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:19.831
It's right here on the bed,
man."

00:08:19.831 --> 00:08:23.235
-"I'm here. Right here.
Why don't you see me?"

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:27.006
-Last thing, I know
this is a question I'm asking

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:29.575
knowing full well
you'll avoid it, but phase 5

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.577
of Marvel is very exciting
-Very exciting.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:34.112
-Young Avengers.
People talk about the idea

00:08:34.112 --> 00:08:35.814
of Young Avengers.
-What are you talking about?

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:38.650
-I'm just saying if
there was going to be something

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.152
like that,
would you be interested?

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.854
-I don't know. Would I?
I mean, like, what?

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:45.757
The thing that's cool was making
this movie was the best project

00:08:45.757 --> 00:08:47.593
of my life, and even if
I'm lucky enough to do

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:49.495
another Marvel movie,
nothing will ever top

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.996
working with Paul Rudd
everyday.

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:53.232
-There you go.
-Ever. So, I don't know.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.200
-Alright, well,
we're certainly happy

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.103
you made time for us,
on your birthday no less.

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:58.604
-[ Laughs ] On my birthday.

